      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “optimal adjustment” as “the best possible adaptation.” It discusses promoting “optimal adjustment” and reporting that adjustment benefits from a we-perspective and conjoint dyadic coping, but it does not provide support for the evaluative wording “best possible.”",
        "The packet supports “adaptation/adjustment” in couples facing specific dyadic challenges, but the definition’s phrasing “stresses and relationship changes linked to” is broader than what is directly stated (the packet enumerates dyadic challenges such as changed roles, altered communication, compromised sexual intimacy, and reduced social participation)."
